			"statement": "Calcule la somme $S=1+2+2^2+2^3+\\cdots+2^{ {{n}} }$.\n\n$S=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "4..10"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Pour $q\\neq1$ : $1+q+q^2+\\cdots+q^n=\\dfrac{q^{n+1}-1}{q-1}$ (il y a $n+1$ termes).",
					"Ici $q=2$ et le dernier exposant est $\\mathbf{ {{n}} }$ :",
					"$$S=\\dfrac{2^{ {{eval:n+1}} }-1}{2-1}=\\dfrac{ {{eval:2^(n+1)}}-1}{1}={{eval:2^(n+1)-1}}$$"
				]
			}
		},
		{
